ly hall"},{"surface":"தூங்கும்","parts":[{"text":"தூங்கும்","lemma":"தூங்கு","gloss":"hanging"}],"gloss":"hanging"},{"surface":"விசியுறு","parts":[{"text":"விசி","lemma":"விசி","gloss":"tight binding"},{"text":"உறு","lemma":"உறு","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"tightly bound"},{"surface":"தண்ணுமை","parts":[{"text":"தண்ணுமை","lemma":"தண்ணுமை","gloss":"drum"}],"gloss":"drum"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வளி","parts":[{"text":"வளி","lemma":"வளி","gloss":"wind"}],"gloss":"wind"},{"surface":"பொரு","parts":[{"text":"பொரு","lemma":"பொரு","gloss":"strike/beat"}],"gloss":"striking"},{"surface":"தெண்கண்","parts":[{"text":"தெண்கண்","lemma":"தெண்கண்","gloss":"tight drumhead"}],"gloss":"tight drumhead","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கேட்பின்","parts":[{"text":"கேள்","lemma":"கேள்","gloss":"hear"},{"text":"பின்","lemma":"பின்","gloss":"if/when"}],"gloss":"if heard"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அது","parts":[{"text":"அது","lemma":"அது","gloss":"that"}],"gloss":"that"},{"surface":"போர்","parts":[{"text":"போர்","lemma":"போர்","gloss":"battle/war"}],"gloss":"battle"},{"surface":"என்னும்","parts":[{"text":"என்னும்","lemma":"என்","gloss":"saying/called"}],"gloss":"saying"},{"surface":"என்னையும்","parts":[{"text":"என்னை","lemma":"என்னை","gloss":"my lord/leader"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"my lord also"},{"surface":"உளனே","parts":[{"text":"உளன்","lemma":"உள்","gloss":"exists-he"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"indeed exists"}]}],"literal":"Jewel adornment shining rising curved waist / gentle painted-eye bright-forehead songstress / 'Are there warriors also in your wide-placed country?' saying / O king of the fighting army who does not cease asking! / Like a snake that does not fear a striking stick / young, strong warriors also exist; not only that, / hanging in the public assembly hall, tightly bound drum's / wind-striking tight drumhead if heard, / 'That is battle!' saying, my lord also indeed exists.","translation":"O king of the fighting army, who never ceases to ask the gentle songstress with painted eyes, bright forehead, and a curved waist adorned with shining jewels, 'Are there any warriors in your wide country?' There are young, strong warriors here who, like snakes, do not fear the striking stick. Not only that, if they hear the wind beating against the tight head of the drum hanging in the public assembly hall, they cry, 'That is the call to battle!'—and my lord, too, is there!","modern":"ஒளிரும் அணிகலன்கள் அணிந்த, உயர்ந்த அல்குலை உடைய, மென்மையான, மை தீட்டிய கண்களையும் பிரகாசமான நெற்றியையும் கொண்ட விறலியிடம், 'உன்னுடைய அகன்ற நாட்டில் போர் வீரர்களும் இருக்கிறார்களா?' என்று ஓயாமல் கேட்கும் போர்முனை வேந்தனே! அடிக்கும் கோலுக்கு அஞ்சாத பாம்பைப் போன்ற இளமையும் வலிமையும் மிக்க வீரர்கள் இங்கு இருக்கிறார்கள். அதுமட்டுமல்லாமல், பொதுமன்றத்தில் தொங்கும், இறுக்கமாகக் கட்டப்பட்ட தண்ணுமையில் காற்று மோதி ஒலிக்கும் சத்தத்தைக் கேட்டாலே, 'அது போர் முரசு!' என்று கிளம்பும் என் தலைவனும் இருக்கிறான்.","explanation":"The poet Avvaiyār addresses an invading king who mockingly asks a songstress if there are any real warriors in her land. Avvaiyār proudly replies that her country is full of young, fierce warriors who, like cobras, do not shrink from a raised stick. Furthermore, she highlights the extreme valor of her lord, Atiyamāṉ, stating that even the sound of the wind rustling the drum hanging in the village common hall makes him rise up, thinking it is the call to war. This poem belongs to the tumpai tiṇai, which celebrates the battlefield valor of warriors. The key words are 'மள்ளர்' (warriors), 'அரவு' (snake), 'தண்ணுமை' (drum), and 'என்னை' (my lord).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}